1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,800
Everyone drives the G318 to Tibet. Skip it. I'm your China Travel Expert.

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:05,200
The G318 runs 2,142 km, Chengdu to Lhasa.

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:07,600
Ten to twelve days, over passes above 5,000 metres.

4
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:10,000
And foreigners need two Tibet permits to drive it.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,400
The road I'd pick instead? Xinjiang's Duku Highway.

6
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:15,000
561 km across the Tianshan, no Tibet permit.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,400
Desert, canyons, alpine meadows, snow, in one day.

8
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:20,000
Double-tap if you'd take the Duku over the G318.

9
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,400
The catch: it opens only about four months a year.

10
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:25,400
★ Expert Tip: drive the Duku June to September; it closes with the snow.

11
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:28,200
G318 or Duku — which drive are you making? Tell me below.
